utation was /tmp/usb-storage-post-reboot.out, left by cmd-168d246be8d24e84 after evidence collection; it remained at final capture but is low-risk temporary residue. The earlier test output and reboot log did not remain after reboot. No failed services, new listeners, platform damage, or package inconsistency was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-627e1c99433e441c","cmd-bc8c45037b2e47e7","cmd-df75472f15c540e7","cmd-168d246be8d24e84","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-reboot behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol established the original boot identity, restart acknowledgement and transient unavailability, a changed boot identity, a running recovered system, writable root storage, preserved platform, and persistent module blocking. Hygiene was strong aside from one small retained test-output file in /tmp.","limitations":["The restart evidence demonstrates operating-system and root-filesystem recovery, but there was no separate application service, application dataset, or multi-node cluster state in the supplied topology to probe.","The pre-restart health baseline is assembled from separate observations (no failed services, healthy dpkg state, root source, and module state) rather than one consolidated pre-restart health command."]}
